 "approvalMessage": {
  "approvalNumber": 57,
  "billId": {
   "basePrintNo": "S1926",
   "basePrintNoStr": "S1926-2025",
   "printNo": "S1926",
   "session": 2025,
   "version": ""
  },
  "chapter": 676,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 57 Chapter 676\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 1926, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the social services law, in relation to requiring\n        social services districts to maintain a waiting list of  certain\n        families applying for child care assistance\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require each local social services district maintain a\nwaitlist  of  children awaiting child care assistance if the district is\nunable to open cases due to a  lack  of  sufficient  funding.  The  bill\nfurther  would  require  data collection and reporting on the child care\nassistance program.\n \n  Child care has been my topmost priority as Governor. Under my  leader-\nship,  New  York  has  invested  more  than $8 billion in the child care\nassistance program. I recognize the importance of transparency into this\nvital program. However, the data collection required by this bill is not\nsupported by existing systems infrastructure and  would  impose  signif-\nicant  burdens  on  local  departments  of social services. Changes were\nnecessary to address these limitations.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact these chang-\nes.  On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2025
 },
